{
  "id": "COMPOUND:19233 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Trichothecolone is implicated in the target pathway leading to SNB-78 through multiple intermediate compounds, all of which are known targets of SNU-387, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside. These intermediates suggest a complex metabolic cascade where Trichothecolone may act as a precursor or modulator in the activation of these compounds, which in turn target SNB-78. The shared target SNB-78 implies a potential mechanism of action involving the activation of downstream pathways, possibly through the production or modification of these intermediates. The evidence supports a relationship where Trichothecolone may influence the activity of these compounds, which then interact with SNB-78, highlighting a possible role in the broader pharmacological profile of Trichothecolone.",
